          deckDescription: 'One 32-card German-suited deck: four suits (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells) with eight ranks per suit (7, 8, 9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace). Used for Dudak and similar games; created by removing the 6s and lower from a full German pack. No jokers.',
          suitDescription: 'Four German suits: Acorns (Eichel), Leaves (Laub), Hearts (Herz), Bells (Schellen), each with eight cards. Trump and lead rules depend on the variant; follow suit when able. Card order and point values follow the regional 32-card convention for trick-taking.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit from low to high: 7, 8, 9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace. Point values typically follow Ace-Ten scoring (Ace 11, Ten 10, King 4, Ober 3, Unter 2, numerals 0). Strength and trick order are as in standard 32-card German games.',
